235
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:31,240
family. The first important difference is in the man's role.

236
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:35,980
The traditional husband was the head of the household because he was the only one

237
00:23:35,980 --> 00:23:37,420
who worked outside the home.

238
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:42,300
If the wife worked for pay then the husband was not considered to be a good

239
00:23:42,300 --> 00:23:48,100
provider. In many families today both husband and wife work for pay.

240
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:50,780
Therefore they share the role of head of household.

241
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:56,280
In addition the traditional husband usually made the big decisions about spending

242
00:23:56,280 --> 00:24:01,880
money. However the modern husband shares these decisions with his working wife.

243
00:24:02,420 --> 00:24:06,920
Also the traditional husband did not help his wife with the housework or meal

244
00:24:06,920 --> 00:24:10,080
preparation. Dinner was ready when he came home.

245
00:24:10,340 --> 00:24:14,400
In contrast the modern husband helps his working wife at home.

246
00:24:14,980 --> 00:24:19,900
He may do some of the household jobs and it is not unusual for him to cook.

247
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:22,980
The second difference is in the woman's role.

248
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:28,100
In the traditional family the woman may have worked for pay during her first years

249
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:33,500
of marriage. However after she became pregnant she would usually give up her job.

250
00:24:34,020 --> 00:24:37,020
Her primary role was to take care of her family.

251
00:24:37,460 --> 00:24:42,940
In contrast in many families today the modern woman works outside the home even

252
00:24:42,940 --> 00:24:44,260
after she has children.

253
00:24:44,860 --> 00:24:49,660
She's doing two jobs instead of one so she is busier than the traditional mother

254
00:24:49,660 --> 00:24:54,680
was. The traditional wife learned to live within her husband's income.

255
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:59,500
However the modern wife does not have to live within her husband's income because

256
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:01,480
the family has two incomes.

257
00:25:02,100 --> 00:25:04,660
The final difference is in the role of the children.

258
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:09,840
In the traditional family the children were taken care of by the mother because she

259
00:25:09,840 --> 00:25:11,600
did not work outside the home.

260
00:25:12,420 --> 00:25:18,660
However today preschool children may go to a childcare center or to a babysitter

261
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:21,300
regularly because the mother works.

262
00:25:21,860 --> 00:25:25,780
The school age children of a traditional family were more dependent.

263
00:25:26,320 --> 00:25:30,820
Their mother was there to help them to get ready for school and to make their

264
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:35,060
breakfast. In contrast modern children are more independent.

265
00:25:35,580 --> 00:25:39,180
They have to get up early in the morning and get ready for school.

266
00:25:39,180 --> 00:25:44,460
Their mother is busy getting ready for work so they may even have to make their own

267
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:50,340
breakfast. In conclusion the American family today is quite different from the

268
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:51,920
family of 50 years ago.

269
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:58,100
In the modern family the roles of the father mother and children have changed as

270
00:25:58,100 --> 00:26:00,580
more and more women work outside the home.

271
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:06,300
The next century may bring more important changes to the American family structure.

